From: lg <lgpay@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] fs: clamp max_fd in the close_range() backport

The 5.9 close_range() backport is missing upstream's fd-table clamp, so
close_range(3, ~0U, 0) loops forever inside the syscall. Android bionic never
calls it; glibc/systemd inside containers do, which hangs systemd at boot.

---
 fs/file.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

--- a/fs/file.c
+++ b/fs/file.c
@@ -705,6 +705,11 @@
 static inline void __range_close(struct files_struct *cur_fds, unsigned int fd,
 				 unsigned int max_fd)
 {
+	/* Make sure we're using the correct maximum value. */
+	spin_lock(&cur_fds->file_lock);
+	max_fd = min(last_fd(files_fdtable(cur_fds)), max_fd);
+	spin_unlock(&cur_fds->file_lock);
+
 	while (fd <= max_fd) {
 		struct file *file;
 
